 # Windows setup
 
-PiG supports source builds on Windows. Do not treat Windows as release-supported until native release verification passes for the published artifact.
+PiG supports Windows on amd64. Release archives and npm packages for windows/arm64 are published, but they have no native smoke test, so treat arm64 as unverified.
+
+If PiG behaves differently from Pi on Windows, that is a bug or a documented divergence. [Differences from Pi on Windows](#differences-from-pi-on-windows) lists the documented ones.
+
+## Install
+
+In PowerShell:
+
+```powershell
+irm https://pi-in-go.dev/install.ps1 | iex
+```
+
+With npm:
+
+```powershell
+npm install -g @pi-in-go/pig
+```
+
+With Go:
+
+```powershell
+go install github.com/MichaelKinsy/PiG/cmd/pig@latest
+```
+
+You can also download the `windows-amd64` or `windows-arm64` zip from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/MichaelKinsy/PiG/releases). The `install.sh` installer supports macOS and Linux only. If SmartScreen or `PATH` gets in the way, see [install troubleshooting](/docs/latest/install-troubleshooting).
 
