-## Verification
+## Differences from Pi on Windows
 
-Run the Windows-native unit and integration gates before claiming support for an artifact. A Linux cross-build alone does not prove Windows terminal, process, filesystem, update, or extension behavior.
+- A standalone `pig.exe` does not replace itself (D39). Run the installer again, or download the new zip. npm and pnpm installations update through their package manager, as in Pi.
+- Pi's suspend key reports "Suspend to background is not supported on Windows". PiG does the same.
+- A Node extension connects to the host over a named pipe that only the current user can open. Go, Python and Rust extensions use AF_UNIX. Extension code does not see the difference.
+- Files that must be readable only by their owner, such as Piglet secrets, are protected with a Windows ACL instead of POSIX mode bits (D68).
+- Container builds of a Piglet do not pass `--user`. The image's default user runs the build (D67).
+- `pig piglet build --format script` writes a `.cmd` launcher on Windows (D69).
 
